      "heading": "Putting it together",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Broad O–H and C double bond O: a carboxylic acid.",
          "write": "IR: –COOH"
        },
        {
          "say": "Three carbons, one near 180 ppm. An ethyl group in proton NMR.",
          "write": "¹³C + ¹H"
        },
        {
          "say": "So it is propanoic acid, CH three CH two COOH.",
          "write": "CH₃CH₂COOH"
        },
        {
          "say": "Check: 36 plus 6 plus 32 is 74. It matches M plus.",
          "write": "M = 74.0 ✓"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Watch out for these",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "The tallest peak is the base peak, not the molecular ion.",
          "write": "base ≠ M⁺"
        },
        {
          "say": "In the n plus 1 rule, only count neighbouring hydrogens.",
          "write": "neighbours only"
        },
        {
          "say": "Look for symmetry when counting environments.",
          "write": "symmetry"
        },
        {
          "say": "Fragments are positive ions. Write the plus charge.",
          "write": "CH₃CO⁺"
        }
      ]
